<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<article>
    <title>Introduction to XML and Markdown</title>
    <section>
        <h1>What is XML?</h1>
        <p>XML (<strong>eXtensible Markup Language</strong>) is a markup language that defines a set of rules for encoding documents in a format that is both human-readable and machine-readable.</p>
        
        <h2>Key Features of XML</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Platform independent</li>
            <li>Support for Unicode</li>
            <li>Hierarchical structure representation</li>
        </ul>
        
        <p>Here's a sample XML code:</p>
        <pre>
&lt;person&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;John Smith&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;age&gt;35&lt;/age&gt;
&lt;/person&gt;
        </pre>
    </section>
    
    <section>
        <h1>Converting to Markdown</h1>
        <p>This document demonstrates conversion from XML to <em>Markdown</em>.</p>
        
        <h2>Images in XML</h2>
        <p>Here's an example of an image in XML:</p>
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Sample Icon" />
        
        <p>And a reference to <a href="https://example.com">an external website</a>.</p>
    </section>
</article>
